      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, that's definitely sounding a bit more upbeat. I just ran it through the tool again and it climbed up to about a 0.65. We're getting closer to the \"safe\" zone, but management is still being really difficult about the \"incident\" and \"investigation\" wording. They feel like those words themselves are driving the sentiment score down, even if the surrounding sentences are positive.\n\nCan we try one more version? See if you can get us into that 0.8+ range. I still need you to be careful with legal, but try to lean even more into the \"commitment to excellence\" and \"enhancing the guest experience\" angle. Maybe focus less on the actual problem and more on our positive response and our bright future with these new improvements? Like, instead of focusing on the \"incident,\" focus on our \"dedicated pursuit of world-class standards.\" \n\nJust try to hit that high score without making it look like we're ignoring the guests who actually got sick.",
